      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right to look past the joke; intermittent hardware faults like a failing power supply on a switch can indeed cause bizarre traffic patterns by momentarily dropping voltage or reset signals. A device might successfully transmit packets for a few seconds before the flicker causes the controller to drop connection abruptly, creating the massive latency spikes you see at Hop 3. These events are often invisible to standard logs because the packet loss happens below the driver's actual detection threshold or gets consolidated into a single lost frame count before it reaches your monitoring system.",
